# The build context is the whole repository, because the worker compiles the shared packages.
# Without this file `fly deploy` uploads node_modules and every stored capture — the evidence
# directory alone is tens of megabytes per run, and none of it belongs in the image.
#
# Evidence in particular must never be baked into a container. It lives in the private Supabase
# bucket; a copy inside an image would be a second, unversioned, publicly-pullable copy of a
# merchant's captures.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — the image compiles its own.
dist
**/dist
out
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local run artifacts.
#
# apps/web/public/{evidence,reports} are symlinked local output (see `npm run link-runs`). They
# must be excluded explicitly now that apps/web is part of the build context — otherwise every
# stored merchant capture would be baked into a pullable container image.
evidence
reports
.tmp
apps/web/public/evidence
apps/web/public/reports
apps/web/dist

# Never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Not used by the worker.
#
# apps/web is NOT excluded: the worker prints the report route to make a PDF, so the container
# builds the frontend. `brand/` goes with it — the print header carries the lockup, and a PDF
# with a broken image where the mark should be is not a document anyone sends to an underwriter.
apps/web/dist-types
apps/testbed
demo
fixtures
docs
*.md
